WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.830
Antarctica has no police of its own,
and no penalty system of its own.

2
00:00:04.880 --> 00:00:07.950
Yet 58 countries are party to one treaty,

3
00:00:08.000 --> 00:00:11.790
covering everywhere south
of 60 degrees South.

4
00:00:11.840 --> 00:00:13.610
Fishing boats work these waters.

5
00:00:13.660 --> 00:00:15.750
Commercial whaling is paused.

6
00:00:15.800 --> 00:00:17.510
Mining is banned.

7
00:00:17.560 --> 00:00:21.250
So with no one on patrol,
how are these rules enforced?

8
00:00:21.300 --> 00:00:24.210
Does each claimant police its own slice?

9
00:00:24.260 --> 00:00:27.230
In this mission, you'll take
apart four sets of rules,

10
00:00:27.280 --> 00:00:30.450
from the treaty to the
fisheries convention.

11
00:00:30.500 --> 00:00:33.010
Then you'll judge each one by its purpose,

12
00:00:33.060 --> 00:00:37.470
its scope and its enforcement,
and see what pressure groups add.

13
00:00:37.520 --> 00:00:41.290
Your mission: explain how
Antarctica's rules are made to stick,

14
00:00:41.340 --> 00:00:43.470
with no police on patrol.
